            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0198" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg124"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>No official record of this meeting has been found. Hull (vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 1121–1122) says: “Following the meeting
                    [with Churchill] the President called in Soviet Ambassador Litvinov and handed
                    him a copy [of the Joint Declaration] to be sent immediately to his Government
                        <pb facs="0199" n="125" xml:id="pg125"/> for comment.” See also the
                    statement by Hull in his memorandum of conversation of December 29, 1941, in
                        <ref target="frus:frus1942v01/pg_18">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 18</ref>. The text of the draft as
                    given to Litvinov is in telegram 6081 of December 28 from Halifax to Eden, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg370">p. 370</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
